  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### 1c. Negative check: combining the two families\n\nApply (a) then a family-(b)-type factor (gamma + delta t1(th1)^-1), and (b) then (a), and (a) twice, to W_a^2 at the same exact point (generic alpha, beta, gamma, delta). Shown: singular-value ratio sigma2/sigma1 of the site-s flattening (0 iff site s factorises). If every site factorises the state is a product state; the test is whether the *site vectors* of the final bra coincide with a two-parameter product v(a1 + b1 Lambda^-1) (x) u(a2 + b2 Lambda), which would need a state of the form (pair-1 sites rotated by independent polynomials).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "ngNeg[sv_, th_, z_] := Module[{bra = ngProd[sv], T1a, T1b, ya, yab, yba, yaa, dflt, I4 = IdentityMatrix[4], fa, fb, sd},\n   T1a = ngT1[th, z, th[[1]]]; T1b = ngT1[th, z, th[[2]]];\n   fa[x_, al_, be_] := al ngInvAct[x, T1a] + be ngInvAct[x, T1a] . T1b;\n   fa[x_, al_, be_] := Module[{y = ngInvAct[x, T1a]}, al y + be (y . T1b)];\n   fb[x_, ga_, de_] := ga x + de ngInvAct[x, T1a];\n   ya = fa[bra, 3/5, -2/7]; yab = fb[ya, 2/3, 5/11]; yba = fa[fb[bra, 2/3, 5/11], 3/5, -2/7]; yaa = fa[ya, 1/3, 4/9];\n   sd[b_] := Table[With[{sv2 = SingularValueList[N[ngFlat[b, s]]]}, If[Length[sv2] < 2, 0., sv2[[2]]/sv2[[1]]]], {s, 4}];\n   {{\"(a) alone\", sd[ya]}, {\"(a) then (b)\", sd[yab]}, {\"(b) then (a)\", sd[yba]}, {\"(a) twice\", sd[yaa]}}];\nngNegRes = ngNeg[ngRefW, ngTh0, ngZ0];\nGrid[Prepend[Map[{#[[1]], Sequence @@ (ScientificForm[#, 3] & /@ #[[2]])} &, ngNegRes], {\"bra\", \"site 1\", \"site 2\", \"site 3\", \"site 4\"}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
