  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 6. Negative statement: which pair-1 configurations are reached\n\nTrace v.u of the pair vectors of the limit bras (finite-eps A site e1 + a (z1/z4) e4 and the like tend to the vectors below): family (a): (e1 + a e4, e4 - a' e1), trace a - a'; family (b): (e1 + a'' e4, e4 - a e1), trace a'' - a; chain: pair 1 = W_a (trace 0, unchanged), pair 2 as in (a). The even-bridge target W_a' (a' != a, traceless) has A = e1 + a' e4 and F = e4 - a' e1: to be reached the limit needs both the A and the F site of the same pair rotated consistently, i.e. both families at once, which section 1c shows is not a product state (and, in the chain, the fixed rotations are trivial in the limit).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "ngTr[v_, u_] := v . u;\nngNegRows = Module[{a = 1/3, cp = 2., phi = ngPhi1, ap, app},\n   ap = a (cp + phi[[1]])/(cp + phi[[4]]); app = a (cp + phi[[4]])/(cp + phi[[1]]);\n   {{\"(a): pair 1 = (e1 + a e4, e4 - a' e1)\", N[ap], ngTr[ngE[1] + a ngE[4], ngE[4] - ap ngE[1]], \"= a - a'\"},\n    {\"(b): pair 1 = (e1 + a'' e4, e4 - a e1)\", N[app], ngTr[ngE[1] + app ngE[4], ngE[4] - a ngE[1]], \"= a'' - a\"},\n    {\"chain: pair 1 = W_a\", N[a], ngTr[ngE[1] + a ngE[4], ngE[4] - a ngE[1]], \"trace 0, a unchanged; pair 2 as (a)\"},\n    {\"even-bridge target: pair 1 = W_a', a' != a\", \"-\", 0, \"requires A and F rotated together: not reached\"}}];\nGrid[Prepend[ngNegRows, {\"configuration\", \"a' or a''\", \"v.u\", \"comment\"}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
