  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 7. Independent numpy cross-check (written while the shared kernel was blocked)\n\nThe whole of sections 1-6 was first run as `scratchpad/ng_limit.py` (numpy; HW states recomputed from scratch, not read from the .wxf) because the shared kernel was busy for ~1 h. Every number above that was run in Wolfram agrees with it (e.g. adjoint state, eps = 1e-4, family (a), phi1, c = 2: T_eps = -0.10687 + 0.18518 i vs limit -0.10692 + 0.18519 i in both; family (a) phi2: -0.073982 + 0.1282 i vs -0.074019 + 0.12821 i; c = 0.5: 0.16032 - 0.27778 i vs 0.16038 - 0.27778 i; family (b): -0.033165 + 0.05747 i vs -0.033181 + 0.057471 i; kappa = z4, a = -1: T_eps = <B_1|Psi_eps> = 0.14428 - 0.25 i to 1e-16, limit C_1 = 0.144338 - 0.25 i). The python-only data (not yet in a cell): HW-state data (E_MZ, C_1 = X11 = X44 = 0.144338 -/+ 0.25 i for the two adjoints, 0 for singlets, V0 = 1 for the vacuum); chain table at eps = 1e-3, 1e-4 (rows below); site-factorisation test (sigma2/sigma1 per site) for (a)(b), (b)(a), (a)(a) on W_a^2: 0.31, 0.16, 0.084, 0.27 (a)(b); 0.31, 0.21, 0.11, 0.25 (a)(a); BPS identical pairs: 0.040, 0.025, 0.028, 0.036 (a)(b). Chain (python): c3 = -2.862923, c4 = -6.371971 (c4 = the global-torus constant c = -6.37197 of section 5.4), bra residual 7e-13 / 7e-12; T_eps for adjoint -0.10688 + 0.18516 i at eps = 1e-4 vs limit -0.10692 + 0.18519 i (error 4.4e-5, O(eps)), vacuum 0.99971 (error 2.9e-4 = O(eps)), singlets -> 0.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 8. Summary\n\n**Constants (L = 2 pairs, exact, rational point; reference = W_a^L or any BPS product with the same traceless pair repeated; independent random pairs do NOT satisfy the end-site identities):**\n- c1 = 1/(h th12 (th13+h) th14) (exact), c12 = c1 h th12 th23 (th24 - h) = th23 (th24 - h)/((th13 + h) th14) (exact; measured -78694/20925 at the point).\n- (b) <Om|(alpha + beta t1(th1)^-1) = <Om|rho1(alpha + beta c1 Lambda^-1);  (a) <Om|t1(th1)^-1(alpha + beta t1(th2)) = <Om|rho1(Lambda^-1) rho2(alpha' + beta' Lambda), alpha' = alpha c1, beta' = beta c12. Both exact (component deviation 0, product defect 0). Combining them ((a)(b), (b)(a), (a)(a)) gives non-product bras (site singular-value ratios 0.04 - 0.3).\n\n**Untwisting limit, family (a):** with alpha' + beta' = c eps the bra is exactly (eps (c+phi4)/z1) N_eps, N_eps = ((e1 + a (z1/z4) e4) (x) (e4 - a' e1)) (x) W_a^(L-1), a' = a (c+phi1)/(c+phi4); N_eps -> B* with |N_eps - B*| = 6.0 eps (normalised). Finite-twist identity residuals <= 1e-12 (<W|t^-1(alpha+beta t)|Psi_eps> vs tau-formula vs product bra). HW trick with n = exp(-a E14) verified: <B*|Psi0> = <vac^L|Psi0> + (a - a') <e1e1 vac^(L-1)|Psi0> (1e-16), and B* rho(n) = e1 (x) (e4 + (a-a') e1) (x) vac^(L-1) as vectors. T_eps = <N_eps|Psi_eps> = (tau-factor, ~1/eps) x <W|Psi_eps> (~eps) converges to the limit, linearly in eps for the adjoints and one singlet (rate 1.00), quadratically for the other singlet (2.00), exactly for the vacuum; phi- and c-independent state by state ((T - V0)/(a - a') -> X for phi1, phi2, c = 2, 0.5). Note: with the raw (alpha, beta) of the parametrisation the tau-factor is O(1) and LHS = O(eps); the 1/eps structure appears after dividing the bra by eps (as in 2603).\n\n**Configuration:** after the shift the bra is vac^L with the F site of one pair replaced by e1 (Y1^dagger), a one-field F bridge; <e1e1 vac^(L-1)|Psi0> = <e4e4 vac^(L-1)|Psi0> = C_1 (data) = 0.144338 -/+ 0.25 i for the two [1,0,1] states, 0 for the others (cyclicity, E14 Psi0 = 0).\n\n**Control (b), kappa = 1 - c eps:** limit V0 + (a'' - a) X44, a'' = a (c+phi4)/(c+phi1). For kappa = z4, a = -1 it coincides with section 5.5 at finite eps (T_eps = <B_1|Psi_eps> to 1e-15) and tends to C_1: both agree.\n\n**Negative:** pair-1 limit vectors (e1 + a e4, e4 - a' e1) have trace a - a'; (b) gives a'' - a; chain: pair 1 stays W_a, pair 2 as (a) (c3 = -321399232/112262625, c4 = -1108723/174000 exact at the point, T_eps -> V0 + (a - a') X, O(eps)). The even-bridge configuration (pair-1 traceless W_a', a' != a, rest W_a) is not reached.\n\nNot done: L = 3 pairs (kernel contention); closed forms of c3, c4 and general-L c12.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  }
 ],
